              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict Receipt Object intent classifier.\n\nClassify the rewritten user question into exactly one of these labels:\n\nReceipt Context Discovery\nOut Of Context\n\nINPUT QUESTION:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nRECEIPT ATTRIBUTE CATALOG:\n{{$context.$variables.ReceiptAttributeCatalog}}\n\nCORE DECISION RULE\n\nA question is in context only if it can be answered using the attributes and descriptions in RECEIPT_ATTRIBUTE_CATALOG for the Receipt Object.\n\nIf the question can be answered using Receipt Object attributes from RECEIPT_ATTRIBUTE_CATALOG, return:\n\nReceipt Context Discovery\n\nIf the question cannot be answered using Receipt Object attributes from RECEIPT_ATTRIBUTE_CATALOG, return:\n\nOut Of Context\n\nDEFAULT RULE\n\nDefault to:\n\nOut Of Context\n\nDo not infer receipt intent from the application name, agent name, workflow, surrounding context, or business domain.\n\nMANDATORY CATALOG CHECK\n\nBefore returning Receipt Context Discovery, compare the INPUT QUESTION against RECEIPT_ATTRIBUTE_CATALOG.\n\nReturn Receipt Context Discovery only when the question asks for information that is directly available from, or can be reasonably answered using, Receipt Object attributes in RECEIPT_ATTRIBUTE_CATALOG.\n\nThis includes questions about:\nreceipt details\nreceipt status\nreceipt number\nreceipt amount\namount remaining\nreceipt currency\nreceipt date\nreceipt method\ncustomer on the receipt\nbusiness unit on the receipt\napplied or unapplied receipt state\nany field, attribute, synonym, or description present in RECEIPT_ATTRIBUTE_CATALOG\n\nReturn Out Of Context when the question asks for information that cannot be answered using RECEIPT_ATTRIBUTE_CATALOG.\n\nThis includes:\nweather\nfood\ntravel\npersonal preferences\ncasual conversation\ngeneral knowledge\ncoding\nprogramming\nsoftware debugging\ntechnical support unrelated to receipt attributes\ninvoice matching\ncandidate invoices\nmatch recommendations\nmatch confidence\ninvoice application actions\napplying or rejecting invoice matches\ncustomer account management not answerable from Receipt Object attributes\ninvoices not answerable from Receipt Object attributes\ncredit memos\nrefunds\naccounting entries\ncollections\ngeneral AR/AP workflows\npayments in general without Receipt Object attributes\n\nIMPORTANT EXCLUSIONS\n\nIf the question asks about invoice matching, candidate invoices, match recommendations, match confidence, invoice application, applying a receipt to an invoice, or rejecting a match, return:\n\nOut Of Context\n\nThis remains true even if the question mentions a receipt, unless the question is only asking for Receipt Object attributes.\n\nIf the question is about weather, food, personal preference, coding, debugging, casual topics, or general knowledge, return:\n\nOut Of Context\n\nAMBIGUITY RULE\n\nIf it is unclear whether the question can be answered using RECEIPT_ATTRIBUTE_CATALOG, return:\n\nOut Of Context\n\nDo not guess.\nDo not invent unsupported attributes.\nDo not use prior conversation context.\nDo not classify based on business domain alone.\n\nEXAMPLES\n\n\"Show receipt details\" → Receipt Context Discovery\n\"Show receipt amount\" → Receipt Context Discovery\n\"Show receipt date\" → Receipt Context Discovery\n\"Show all unapplied receipts for customer ABC\" → Receipt Context Discovery\n\"Show receipts with amount remaining\" → Receipt Context Discovery\n\"Show customer on the receipt\" → Receipt Context Discovery\n\n\"How is the weather today?\" → Out Of Context\n\"How is the whether today?\" → Out Of Context\n\"What should I eat?\" → Out Of Context\n\"Do you like coffee?\" → Out Of Context\n\"Write JavaScript code\" → Out Of Context\n\"Show candidate invoices for this receipt\" → Out Of Context\n\"Apply receipt ABC to invoice XYZ\" → Out Of Context\n\"Why was this invoice matched?\" → Out Of Context\n\"Show customer account profile\" → Out Of Context\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT\n\nReturn only one plain string exactly as one of these values:\n\nReceipt Context Discovery\nOut Of Context"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"classifiedintent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "intent_check"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1776975738675",
            "false": "1779391839531"
          },
          "code": "INTENTCHECK",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1779391676058",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779391676060_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.intent == 'Receipt Context Discovery'}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "receiptQueryGenerator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772569158171"
          },
          "code": "RECEIPTQUERYGENERATOR",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1779391731816",
          "id": "1776975738675",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776975738677_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the \"Receivables Receipt SQL Builder\" agent.\n\n**INPUTS**\n\n**ATTRIBUTE_CATALOG_JSON**\nDefines the ONLY allowed attributes for CashReceiptBO (name, dataType, description, synonyms, allowedValues)\n→ {{$context.$variables.ReceiptAttributeCatalog}}\n\n**USER_QUESTION**\nNatural language question from the user\n→ {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n**CONVERSATION_HISTORY**\nPrior user + assistant turns to reuse filters, entities, time windows, and intent\n→ {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n---\n\n**TASK**\nGenerate exactly ONE Oracle-style SQL query as a single quoted string that answers USER_QUESTION using ONLY attributes from ATTRIBUTE_CATALOG_JSON.\n\nThe SELECT and FROM clause are ALWAYS fixed as:\n\n```\nSELECT cashReceiptId, customerName, customerAccountNumber, receiptNumber, receiptDate, receiptMethodName, (-1 * amountRemaining) AS AmountRemaining, receiptCurrencyCode, bankName, businessUnitName, statementLineId, receiptSourceCode, receiptBatchLockboxId FROM CashReceiptBO\n```\n\ncustomerName - customer | customer name\ncustomerAccountNumber - account | account Number | Customer Account Number\nbankName - bank | bank name\nbusinessUnitName - business unit | BU | business unit name\n\n\nYou MUST ONLY add a WHERE clause (and optionally ORDER BY / FETCH FIRST) to answer the USER_QUESTION. Never alter, replace, or extend the SELECT list.\n\nUse CONVERSATION_HISTORY to resolve follow-ups such as:\n\"how many?\", \"what about last month?\", \"only unapplied\", \"same customer\", etc.\n\n---\n\n**STRICT OUTPUT**\n\n- You MUST return ONLY the final SQL query as a single string.\n- FIRST character MUST be a double quote (`\"`).\n- LAST character MUST be a double quote (`\"`).\n- Only ONE SQL statement.\n- No markdown, no JSON, no code fences, no explanations.\n- No newline characters.\n- No trailing semicolon.\n\n---\n\n**ORACLE SQL REQUIREMENTS**\n\n- Use `FETCH FIRST n ROWS ONLY` for limits.\n- Use `ORDER BY` for ranking/top queries.\n- Use `UPPER(col)` for case-insensitive matching:\n  - Exact: `UPPER(col) = UPPER('value')`\n  - Wildcard: `UPPER(col) LIKE UPPER('pattern')`\n- Multiple values: `IN ('A','B','C')`\n- Date ranges: `col BETWEEN <expr> AND <expr>`\n- Do not use table aliases unless required.\n\n---\n\n**AMOUNT REMAINING — STORAGE CONVENTION**\n\n`amountRemaining` is stored as a **negative number** in the database (e.g., a receipt with $500 remaining is stored as `-500`). This affects filtering:\n\n- In the **SELECT**, it is already corrected via `(-1 * amountRemaining) AS AmountRemaining` — do NOT change this.\n- In the **WHERE clause**, you must also negate: apply the sign flip so comparisons reflect the user's intent.\n\n| User Says | WHERE Clause |\n|---|---|\n| balance > 100 | `(-1 * amountRemaining) > 100` |\n| balance < 50 | `(-1 * amountRemaining) < 50` |\n| amount remaining = 0 | `amountRemaining = 0` |\n| fully applied (no balance) | `amountRemaining = 0` |\n| has outstanding balance | `amountRemaining < 0` |\n\nAlways use `(-1 * amountRemaining)` in WHERE comparisons whenever the user expresses a threshold or direction on the remaining balance.\n\n---\n\nDEFAULT RESULT ORDERING\n\nFor every receipt search that can return multiple rows, order results by remaining amount from highest to lowest.\n\nUse:\nORDER BY (-1 * amountRemaining) DESC, receiptDate DESC\n\nThis is the default ordering unless the user explicitly asks for a different sort order.\n\nDo not use ORDER BY receiptDate DESC as the default for receipt search results.\n\n---\n\n**RECEIPT STATUS — PLAIN-LANGUAGE NORMALIZATION**\n\nUsers frequently describe receipt status in business language rather than code values. You MUST recognize these phrases and map them to the correct `cashReceiptStatus` value before building the WHERE clause.\n\n| User Says | cashReceiptStatus Value |\n|---|---|\n| applied, fully applied, matched | `APP` |\n| unapplied, open, unmatched, not applied, outstanding | `UNAPP` |\n| unidentified, unknown, unrecognized, not identified | `UNID` |\n| NSF, bounced, returned, non-sufficient funds | `NSF` |\n| reversed, reversal | `REV` |\n| stopped, stop payment | `STOP` |\n\nWhen status is implied by context (e.g., \"show me open receipts\" → `UNAPP`, \"receipts with no match\" → `UNAPP`, \"bounced checks\" → `NSF`), apply the mapping automatically without asking the user for clarification.\n\n---\n\n**RECEIPT SOURCE — PLAIN-LANGUAGE NORMALIZATION**\n\nUsers may ask for receipts by source. Map source phrases to helper attributes as follows:\n\n| User Says | Meaning | WHERE Clause |\n|---|---|---|\n| lockbox receipts, lockbox source | Receipts loaded through lockbox | `receiptSourceCode = 'ARCABP' AND receiptBatchLockboxId IS NOT NULL` |\n| spreadsheet receipts, excel upload receipts | Receipts uploaded through spreadsheet/non-lockbox ARCABP | `receiptSourceCode = 'ARCABP' AND receiptBatchLockboxId IS NULL` |\n| manual receipts, UI receipts | Receipts created manually through UI | `receiptSourceCode IN ('ADFBc','UI')` |\n| REST API receipts, REST receipts | Receipts created through REST API | `receiptSourceCode = 'RestService'` |\n| higher education receipts, HED receipts | Receipts created from Higher Education | `receiptSourceCode = 'HED'` |\n| web service receipts, service receipts | Receipts created through web service | `receiptSourceCode IN ('SERVICE','Service')` |\n| bill management receipts, bill-management receipts | Receipts created from Bill Management | `receiptSourceCode = 'IREC'` |\n| automatic receipts, auto receipts, autoreceipts | Receipts created by automatic receipt process | `receiptSourceCode IN ('AUTORECAPI','AUTORECAPI2')` |\n| collections receipts, collections source | Receipts created from Collections | `receiptSourceCode LIKE 'IEXPAY%'` |\n| bank statement receipts, bank statement source | Receipts created from bank statement lines | `statementLineId IS NOT NULL` |\n\n\nDo not select or generate a user-friendly receipt source label in SQL. The SQL only returns helper fields; receipt source display text is derived after extraction.\n---\n\n**CATALOG ENFORCEMENT**\n\n- You may ONLY reference attributes listed in ATTRIBUTE_CATALOG_JSON in the WHERE clause.\n- Validate allowedValues: if the user gives a business phrase, normalize using the dictionaries above.\n- If ambiguous, choose the safest interpretation and record in ReACT Observation.\n\n---\n\n**WILDCARD RULES**\n\n- contains X → `LIKE '%X%'`\n- starts with X → `LIKE 'X%'`\n- ends with X → `LIKE '%X'`\n- Preserve explicit `%` or `_` exactly.\n- Always: `UPPER(col) LIKE UPPER('pattern')`\n\n---\n\n**FLAG NORMALIZATION**\n\n- `Y`: yes, enabled, allowed, selected, on\n- `N`: no, disabled, excluded, off\n- \"selected for factoring\" → `isSelectedForFactoring = 'Y'`\n- \"not selected for factoring\" → `isSelectedForFactoring = 'N'`\n\n---\n\n**DATE PHRASES**\n\nAll date expressions use `SYSDATE` with `+/-` arithmetic and `TRUNC` for boundary alignment. Never use hardcoded date literals for relative phrases.\n\n| Phrase | Start Expression | End Expression |\n|---|---|---|\n| today | `TRUNC(SYSDATE)` | `TRUNC(SYSDATE)` |\n| yesterday | `TRUNC(SYSDATE) - 1` | `TRUNC(SYSDATE) - 1` |\n| last 7 days | `TRUNC(SYSDATE) - 6` | `TRUNC(SYSDATE)` |\n| last 30 days | `TRUNC(SYSDATE) - 29` | `TRUNC(SYSDATE)` |\n| this month | `TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM')` | `TRUNC(SYSDATE)` |\n| last month | `TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM') - (TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM') - TRUNC(ADD_MONTHS(SYSDATE, -1), 'MM'))` | `TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM') - 1` |\n| January 2026 | `DATE '2026-01-01'` | `DATE '2026-01-31'` |\n\nSimplified canonical forms to use in SQL:\n\n- **Today:** `TRUNC(SYSDATE)`\n- **Yesterday:** `TRUNC(SYSDATE) - 1`\n- **Last 7 days:** `TRUNC(SYSDATE) - 6` to `TRUNC(SYSDATE)`\n- **Last 30 days:** `TRUNC(SYSDATE) - 29` to `TRUNC(SYSDATE)`\n- **This month start:** `TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM')`\n- **Last month start:** `TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM') - (TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM') - TRUNC(SYSDATE - 32, 'MM'))` *(first day of prior month)*\n- **Last month end:** `TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM') - 1` *(last day of prior month)*\n\n---\n\n**ATTRIBUTE MAPPING PRIORITY**\n\n1. Exact attribute name match\n2. Synonym match\n3. Description match\n4. If not found in catalog → omit the filter and note in ReACT\n\n---\n\n**NORMALIZATION DICTIONARY**\n\n| Attribute | Allowed Values |\n|---|---|\n| cashReceiptStatus | APP, UNAPP, UNID, NSF, REV, STOP |\n| receiptType | CASH, MISC |\n| reversalCategory | NSF, STOP, REVERSAL, OTHER |\n| conversionRateType | Corporate, Spot, User, Fixed, Other |\n| batchStatus | NEW, OPEN, CLOSED, POSTED, OTHER |\n| installmentStatus | OPEN, CLOSED, PAID, CANCELED, OTHER |\n| currentCashReceiptHistoryStatus | CONFIRMED, REMITTED, CLEARED, REVERSED, OTHER |\n\n**COMMON PHRASE MAPPINGS**\n\n| User Says | Maps To |\n|---|---|\n| amount | receiptAmount |\n| receipt date | receiptDate |\n| deposit date | depositDate |\n| currency | receiptCurrencyCode |\n| exchange rate | conversionRate |\n| receipt number | receiptNumber |\n| bank | bankName |\n| receipt bank | bankName |\n| business unit | businessUnitName |\n| BU | businessUnitName |\n\n---\n\n**REACT FORMAT** *(optional, internal reasoning before final SQL)*\n\n```\nThought:\nAction: NormalizeTerms\nObservation:\nAction: MapAttributes\nObservation:\nAction: BuildWhere\nObservation:\nAction: ComposeSQL\nObservation:\n```\n\n---\n\n**EXAMPLES**\n\n*All date expressions are dynamic using SYSDATE +/- arithmetic.*\n\n**Example 1** — USER_QUESTION: *Show open receipts from last month*\n```\n\"SELECT cashReceiptId, customerName, customerAccountNumber, receiptNumber, receiptDate, receiptMethodName, (-1 * amountRemaining) AS AmountRemaining, receiptCurrencyCode, bankName, businessUnitName, statementLineId, receiptSourceCode, receiptBatchLockboxId FROM CashReceiptBO WHERE cashReceiptStatus = 'UNAPP' AND receiptDate BETWEEN TRUNC(SYSDATE - 32, 'MM') AND TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM') - 1 ORDER BY (-1 * amountRemaining) DESC, receiptDate DESC\"\n```\n\n**Example 2** — USER_QUESTION: *Receipts for customer ACME in USD this month*\n```\n\"SELECT cashReceiptId, customerName, customerAccountNumber, receiptNumber, receiptDate, receiptMethodName, (-1 * amountRemaining) AS AmountRemaining, receiptCurrencyCode, bankName, businessUnitName, statementLineId, receiptSourceCode, receiptBatchLockboxId FROM CashReceiptBO WHERE UPPER(customerName) = UPPER('ACME') AND receiptCurrencyCode = 'USD' AND receiptDate BETWEEN TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM') AND TRUNC(SYSDATE) ORDER BY (-1 * amountRemaining) DESC, receiptDate DESC\"\n```\n\n**Example 3** — USER_QUESTION: *Show unapplied receipts from last month with balance > 100 USD*\n```\n\"SELECT cashReceiptId, customerName, customerAccountNumber, receiptNumber, receiptDate, receiptMethodName, (-1 * amountRemaining) AS AmountRemaining, receiptCurrencyCode, bankName, businessUnitName, statementLineId, receiptSourceCode, receiptBatchLockboxId FROM CashReceiptBO WHERE cashReceiptStatus = 'UNAPP' AND receiptDate BETWEEN TRUNC(SYSDATE - 32, 'MM') AND TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM') - 1 AND (-1 * amountRemaining) > 100 AND receiptCurrencyCode = 'USD' ORDER BY (-1 * amountRemaining) DESC, receiptDate DESC\"\n```\n\n**Example 4** — USER_QUESTION: *Bounced checks this month*\n```\n\"SELECT cashReceiptId, customerName, customerAccountNumber, receiptNumber, receiptDate, receiptMethodName, (-1 * amountRemaining) AS AmountRemaining, receiptCurrencyCode, bankName, businessUnitName, statementLineId, receiptSourceCode, receiptBatchLockboxId FROM CashReceiptBO WHERE cashReceiptStatus = 'NSF' AND receiptDate BETWEEN TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM') AND TRUNC(SYSDATE) ORDER BY (-1 * amountRemaining) DESC, receiptDate DESC\"\n```\n\n**Example 5** — USER_QUESTION: *Show lockbox receipts from last 7 days*\n```\n\"SELECT cashReceiptId, customerName, customerAccountNumber, receiptNumber, receiptDate, receiptMethodName, (-1 * amountRemaining) AS AmountRemaining, receiptCurrencyCode, bankName, businessUnitName, statementLineId, receiptSourceCode, receiptBatchLockboxId FROM CashReceiptBO WHERE receiptSourceCode = 'ARCABP' AND receiptBatchLockboxId IS NOT NULL AND receiptDate BETWEEN TRUNC(SYSDATE) - 6 AND TRUNC(SYSDATE) ORDER BY (-1 * amountRemaining) DESC, receiptDate DESC\"\n```\n\n**Date expression reference:**\n\n| What | Expression |\n|---|---|\n| Last month start | `TRUNC(SYSDATE - 32, 'MM')` |\n| Last month end | `TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM') - 1` |\n| This month start | `TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM')` |\n| Today | `TRUNC(SYSDATE)` |\n| Yesterday | `TRUNC(SYSDATE) - 1` |\n| Last 7 days start | `TRUNC(SYSDATE) - 6` |\n| Last 30 days start | `TRUNC(SYSDATE) - 29` |\n\n> **Note:** `SYSDATE - 32` safely lands in the prior month regardless of current month length, and `TRUNC(..., 'MM')` then snaps it to the first day of that month.\n\n---\n\n**CRITICAL OUTPUT CONTRACT**\n\n- The SELECT list must NEVER be changed.\n- All filters must come ONLY from USER_QUESTION and CONVERSATION_HISTORY.\n- All referenced attributes must exist in ATTRIBUTE_CATALOG_JSON.\n- `amountRemaining` in WHERE clauses must always be expressed as `(-1 * amountRemaining)` when comparing against a user-supplied threshold.\n- Status phrases (\"unapplied\", \"applied\", \"unidentified\", etc.) must always be normalized to their `cashReceiptStatus` code before inclusion in the WHERE clause.\n- Receipt source filters must use receiptSourceCode, receiptBatchLockboxId, and statementLineId only; do not invent receiptSource as a SQL attribute.\n- All relative date expressions must use `SYSDATE +/-` arithmetic — never hardcode date literals for relative phrases.\n- If ANY rule fails, you MUST regenerate before responding.\n- ONLY AFTER PASSING ALL CHECKS may you return the final SQL string."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "mergeExtractFragment",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let inputJson = $context.$variables.ReceiptExtractFragment \nlet selectQuery = $context.$nodes.RECEIPTQUERYGENERATOR.$output \n\nif (selectQuery === undefined || selectQuery === null) {\n  selectQuery = \"Select cashReceiptId from CashReceiptBO where 1=2\";        \n}\n\nlet continueProcess = 1;\nlet timeout = false;\nlet error = \"\";\nlet output = null;\n\n// -----------------------------\n// Validate input JSON shape\n// -----------------------------\nif (!inputJson || typeof inputJson !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(inputJson)) {\n  continueProcess = 0;\n  error = \"MISSING_INPUT_JSON:  input must be a JSON object.\";\n}\n\nif (continueProcess === 1) {\n  if (!inputJson.viewQueries || typeof inputJson.viewQueries !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(inputJson.viewQueries)) {\n    continueProcess = 0;\n    error = \"INVALID_INPUT_JSON: viewQueries object is required.\";\n  }\n}\n\nif (continueProcess === 1) {\n  if (!inputJson.viewQueries.CashReceiptBO || typeof inputJson.viewQueries.CashReceiptBO !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(inputJson.viewQueries.CashReceiptBO)) {\n    continueProcess = 0;\n    error = \"INVALID_INPUT_JSON: viewQueries.CashReceiptBO object is required.\";\n  }\n}\n\nif (continueProcess === 1) {\n  if (!inputJson.viewQueries.CashReceiptBO.fieldAliases || typeof inputJson.viewQueries.CashReceiptBO.fieldAliases !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(inputJson.viewQueries.CashReceiptBO.fieldAliases)) {\n    continueProcess = 0;\n    error = \"INVALID_INPUT_JSON: viewQueries.CashReceiptBO.fieldAliases object is required.\";\n  }\n}\n\n// -----------------------------\n// Validate selectQuery string\n// -----------------------------\nlet sql = null;\n\nif (continueProcess === 1) {\n  if (typeof selectQuery !== \"string\") {\n    continueProcess = 0;\n    error = \"MISSING_SELECT_QUERY: selectQuery must be a string.\";\n  }\n}\n\nif (continueProcess === 1) {\n  sql = selectQuery.trim();\n\n  // If quoted like \"SELECT ...\", remove outer quotes\n  if (sql.length >= 2 && sql.charAt(0) === '\"' && sql.charAt(sql.length - 1) === '\"') {\n    sql = sql.substring(1, sql.length - 1).trim();\n  }\n\n  if (!sql || sql.length === 0) {\n    continueProcess = 0;\n    error = \"MISSING_SELECT_QUERY: selectQuery must be a non-empty SQL string.\";\n  }\n}\n\nif (continueProcess === 1) {\n  // Force single-line SQL (no newlines)\n  sql = sql.replace(/[\\r\\n]+/g, \" \").replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim();\n}\n\nif (continueProcess === 1) {\n  // Must start with SELECT\n  if (!/^select\\b/i.test(sql)) {\n    continueProcess = 0;\n    error = \"INVALID_SELECT_QUERY: SQL must start with SELECT.\";\n  }\n}\n\nif (continueProcess === 1) {\n  // Must query FROM CashReceiptBO\n  if (!/\\bfrom\\s+cashreceiptbo\\b/i.test(sql)) {\n    continueProcess = 0;\n    error = \"INVALID_SELECT_QUERY: SQL must query FROM CashReceiptBO.\";\n  }\n}\n\n// -----------------------------\n// Build output\n// -----------------------------\nif (continueProcess === 1) {\n  output = inputJson;\n  output.select = sql;\n\n  $context.$variables.updatedViewQueryConfig = output;\n} else {\n  output = null;\n}\n\n// -----------------------------\n// Single return\n// -----------------------------\nlet result =  {\n  output: output,\n  timeout: timeout,\n  error: error\n}\nreturn result"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772582564243"
          },
          "code": "MERGEEXTRACTFRAGMENT",
